LOK: .uno:SelectObject can enter the marked object's text edit at once

A client that ended a text edit to run a command restores it by
marking the object again; Enter then opens the edit, but Impress
handles Enter by dispatching SID_ATTR_CHAR asynchronously, so a key
that arrives before that dispatch runs meets a marked object that
is not being edited and is lost (Ely R18.8: on a loaded Mac, one
key in two after another program's replace).
SelectObject's LOK branch takes a new Edit argument: with an index,
it marks that object and dispatches SID_ATTR_CHAR synchronously, so
the edit is open when the command returns, its caret where Enter
puts it.
--- a/svx/sdi/svx.sdi
+++ b/svx/sdi/svx.sdi
@@ -8923,7 +8923,7 @@
 
 
 SfxBoolItem SelectObject SID_OBJECT_SELECT
-(SfxUInt32Item Index ID_VAL_INDEX, SfxBoolItem Add FN_PARAM_1)
+(SfxUInt32Item Index ID_VAL_INDEX, SfxBoolItem Add FN_PARAM_1, SfxBoolItem Edit FN_PARAM_2)
 [
     AutoUpdate = TRUE,
     FastCall = FALSE,
--- a/sd/source/ui/view/drviewse.cxx
+++ b/sd/source/ui/view/drviewse.cxx
@@ -174,6 +174,10 @@
             mpDrawView->UnmarkAllObj();
         if (pIndex)
             mpDrawView->MarkObj(aShapes[pIndex->GetValue()], mpDrawView->GetSdrPageView());
+        // Ely: edits in this call, as Enter does later.
+        const SfxBoolItem* pEdit = rReq.GetArg<SfxBoolItem>(FN_PARAM_2);
+        if (pIndex && pEdit && pEdit->GetValue())
+            GetViewFrame()->GetDispatcher()->Execute(SID_ATTR_CHAR, SfxCallMode::SYNCHRON);
         rReq.Done();
         return;
     }
